# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHY this file exists:
#   node_modules/ (6,000+ files), the dist/ build, and release/ binaries had all
#   been committed. That bloated every clone, made diffs unreadable, and meant a
#   stale build could be shipped from the repo instead of rebuilt from source.
#
# RULE OF THUMB: anything a command can regenerate does not belong in git.
#   node_modules/  -> regenerated by `npm ci` from package-lock.json
#   dist/          -> regenerated by `npm run build`
#   release/       -> regenerated by `npm run build:web` / `build:all`
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dependencies — restored exactly from package-lock.json by `npm ci`.
node_modules/

# Build output — Vite writes the single-file game here on `npm run build`.
dist/

# Release artifacts — produced by scripts/build_*.js, attached to GitHub
# Releases instead of being committed.
release/

# Logs from npm, Vite and the verify scripts.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Test and coverage output.
coverage/
.vitest/

# OS junk — created automatically by file managers, never meaningful.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~

# Editor / tool state.
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/

# Tauri's Rust build output (can be many GB).
src-tauri/target/

# Android: Gradle and IDE build output is regenerated by `npx cap sync` and
# Android Studio. The android/ project itself stays tracked.
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
android/.idea/

# The game bundle copied INTO the Android project by `npm run build:android`.
# It is a build output exactly like dist/index.html. A committed copy goes
# stale the moment the game changes -- the one that was committed here predated
# the save system -- so it is regenerated on every Android build instead.
android/app/src/main/assets/public/
